// @@@ For any index 'i' where 0<=i<index, the element at position 'i' in the list is the same as the element at position 'i' in the old list. If the index is not valid, all elements in the list before the index are null and all elements in the old list before the index are also null.

--------------------
// @@@ For any index 'i' in the range of 0 to the removed index, the element at that index in the list is the same as the element at that index in the old list. The removed element is null in both the new list and the old list.

--------------------
// @@@ For any index 'i' that is greater or equal to 0 and less than the current index, the element at position 'i' in the list is null and the previous element at position 'i' was also null, or the element at position 'i' is equal to the previous element at position 'i'.

